WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.802
Learn's Private Access tutorial creates
an application from the custom template,

2
00:00:04.802 --> 00:00:08.156
marks it a Private Access app,
binds it to a connector group,

3
00:00:08.156 --> 00:00:11.650
adds its segments and assigns a
group with the app's user role.

4
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:16.077
Segments may not overlap between
per-app applications; a per-app segment

5
00:00:16.077 --> 00:00:20.725
overrides Quick Access; and clients can
take fifteen minutes to see a change.

6
00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:23.763
Connectors are read with
a write-capable permission

7
00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:26.525
and report active or
inactive, and their version.

8
00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:29.944
Learn's Zero Trust recommendations
ask for two healthy,

9
00:00:29.944 --> 00:00:34.850
current connectors per group, least-privilege
segments and every app assigned.

10
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.290
And for domain controllers,
the sensor starts in audit,

11
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.570
with application service
names before the DC's own.
